Z||000000||hyhy4u||07-16-2001||12:39 PM||||This is a tad off topic at it had to do with my bros 89 Ford Ranger..but its worth posting..My bro in law put on a STP oil filter on there and after about a month the seal on the filter just broke right in two...now if you know his truck you would think something like the oil pan just fell off..lol..so we just didnt worry to much about it and when we did the next oil change we noticed it..what lousy pieces of crap!||||reg||1
Z||000001||KissMySSFiero||07-16-2001||01:56 PM||||that happened on my moms car one time.  i dont recall what kind of filter it was but because it was leaking(thought it was oil pan or something) she figured she was adding oil every other week so she figured theres no need for an oil change.  months went by and she was going to go on a  long trip.  so i was going to do all the normal stuff for a long trip(oil and filter, air filter, etc,,,)  well i took the filter off and whadaya know.  i fixed the oil leak.  i only use delcos on my car and never had a problem. <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierohoho||07-16-2001||02:06 PM||||Could there be people out there who don't know to oil the seal before they put the filter on?<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000003||hyhy4u||07-16-2001||02:46 PM||||Yeah..i usually only use AC Delco stuff..and yeah..ive always oiled the seal before ive put it on.  Now that i think about it i might have one of those crappy STP filters on my fiero..hmm..might have to make a quick oil change this afternoon  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
